# JamfDotNet conventions

- Public API, XML docs, README, and commit-facing text are **English**.
- Packages: `JamfDotNet.Core`, `JamfDotNet.Pro`, `JamfDotNet.Classic`, `JamfDotNet.Platform`, `JamfDotNet.Protect`, `JamfDotNet.School`, `JamfDotNet.TitleEditor`.
- XML docs required on public hand-written members; never rely on Generated XML.
- Never hand-edit `**/Generated/**`. Regenerate via scripts under `scripts/`.
- Do not regenerate Pro/Classic from Platform monolith OpenAPI specs.
- Prefer file-scoped namespaces, nullable reference types, and XML docs on public members.
- Auth and DI helpers live in Core; product packages expose thin façades (Kiota or typed HTTP/GraphQL).
- Protect uses GraphQL at `{base}/app`; School uses Basic + `X-Server-Protocol-Version`.
- Do not hard-code Jamf credentials in source or CI.
- Native AOT is not claimed yet (JSON reflection + Kiota Generated).
